id=a52sxq_media_seccomp_crashdump
name=Galaxy A52s 5G codec HAL seccomp: allow the Android 17 crash_dump syscalls
author=kusti420
description=The Codec2 HALs (vendor.qti.media.c2, samsung.software.media.c2) run under the A14 vendor seccomp policies, which allow exactly what the A14 crash_dump needs. minijail sets NO_NEW_PRIVS, so a native stack dump runs the Android 17 linker's in-process debuggerd fallback under the HAL's own filter, and that code also calls getppid (every backtrace), uname (tombstones) and liblog's setsockopt(SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVTIMEO/SO_SNDTIMEO) / recvfrom (tombstone log section, debuggable builds), so every native stack dump of the codec HALs (each app ANR / watchdog half-trigger / bugreport) kills them: both services restart, running video/audio decoders die (Chrome: "Codec2 component c2.qti.vp9.decoder died", MediaCodec error 1101). Add the missing rules from the system's crash_dump policy. setsockopt is limited to those two options (arg1 == 1 && arg2 == 20/21); verified 2026-10-21 with debuggerd -b, kill -SEGV tombstones and H.264/HEVC/VP9/AV1 playback (no blocked syscall).
